  "chapter": {
    "number": 103,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(104) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Bless the Lord, O my soul. O Lord my God, you are very great; you have clothed yourself with praise and honor:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who do robe yourself with light as with a garment; spreading out the heaven as a curtain.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who covers his chambers with waters; who makes the clouds his chariot; who walks on the wings of the wind.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who makes his angels spirits, and his ministers a flaming fire.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who establishes the earth on her sure foundation: it shall not be moved for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The deep, as it were a garment, is his covering: the waters shall stand",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 194
          },
          {
            "text": "on the hills.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "At your rebuke they shall flee; at the voice of your thunder they shall be alarmed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They go up to the mountains, and down to the plains, to the place which you have founded for them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have set a bound which they shall not pass, neither shall they turn again to cover the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He sends forth his fountains among the valleys: the waters shall run between the mountains.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall give drink to all the wild beasts of the field: the wild asses shall take of them to quench their thirst.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "By them shall the birds of the sky lodge: they shall utter a voice out of the midst of the rocks.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He waters the mountains from his chambers: the earth shall be satisfied with the fruit of your works.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He makes grass to grow for the cattle, and green herb for the service of men, to bring bread out of the earth;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and wine makes glad the heart of man, to make his face cheerful with oil: and bread strengthens man's heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The trees of the plain shall be full of sap; even the cedars of Libanus which he has planted.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There the sparrows will build their nests; and the house of the heron takes the lead among them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The high mountains are a refuge for the stags, and the rock for the rabbits.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knows his going down.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did make darkness, and it was night; in it all the wild beasts of the forest will be abroad:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "even young lions roaring for prey, and to seek meat for themselves from God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The sun arises, and they shall be gathered together, and shall lie down in their dens.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Man shall go forth to his work, and to his labor till evening.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How great are your works, O Lord! in wisdom have you wrought them all: the earth is filled with your creation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So is this great and wide sea: there are things creeping innumerable, small animals and great.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There go the ships; and this dragon whom you have made to play in it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All wait upon you, to give them their food in due season.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When you have given it them, they will gather it; and when you have opened your hand, they shall all be filled with good.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But when you have turned away your face, they shall be troubled: you will take away their breath, and they shall fail, and return to their dust.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall send forth your Spirit, and they shall be created; and you shall renew the face of the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let the glory of the Lord be for ever: the Lord shall rejoice in his works;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 32,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who looks upon the earth, and makes it tremble; who touches the mountains, and they smoke.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 33,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will sing to the Lord while I live; I will sing praise to my God while I exist.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 34,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let my meditation be sweet to him: and I will rejoice in the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 35,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let the sinners fail from off the earth, and transgressors, so that they shall be no more. Bless the Lord, O my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 194,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, above.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 103,
          "verse": 6
        }
      }
    ]
  },
